{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791631322,"nonce":"6kTwaDJKmMMsygAGU0hbLGPsgl8=","title":"Book examples read an animated value once at build time, so they never move","message":"Several book examples pass `value.lock().unwrap().get()` to a setter. That reads the spring once, when the element is built; nothing rebuilds the element as the spring moves, so the property stays where it started.\n\nPages:\n\n- `animation/springs.md`: `.scale(scale.lock().unwrap().get())`, `.left(x..get())`, `.top(y..get())`\n- `components/reusable.md`: `.scale(..get())`, `.opacity(..get())`\n- `components/blinc-component.md`: `.translate_y(..get())`, `.h(height..get())`\n- `getting-started/project-structure.md`: `.transform(Transform::scale(..get()))`, `.opacity(..get())`\n- `architecture/animation.md`: the `ExpandableCard` example, `.h(height..get())`\n\n`motion()` takes the `SharedAnimatedValue` itself (`.scale(value.clone())`), so those calls only need the argument changed. `.left` / `.top` / `.h` on a `Div` take an `f32` or a signal, not a spring, so those examples need reshaping: a `motion().translate_x/y` for position, or a spring-driven signal for height.\n\nThe `motion()` example in `architecture/animation.md` and the `animated_button` example there were fixed alongside the API docs pass.","files":null}]}